# Instructions-only chat: no RE, PR, LF

When the user has **explicitly stated** in this conversation that this chat is for **rules, configuration, or instructions only** (e.g. "this chat is for rule configuration and updates ONLY", "do not process RE/PR/LF here"), then:

- **Do not run** the read-email script or produce the 7-step RE output.
- **Do not run** paste-reply (PR) or log-form (LF) for any customer case.
- If the user types **RE/re**, **PR/pr**, or **LF/lf** in this chat, **do not process** the command. Respond instead:

  **Wrong chat – use the separate agent for customer cases (RE/PR/LF).**

This rule applies only when the user has previously designated the current conversation as instructions-only. It does not affect other chats where RE/PR/LF are used normally.
